APPLE IIGSHP DESKJET PLUS PRINTER DRIVERTESTINGCURRENT AND PREVIOUS RELEASE NOTESBEN KONING-----D6		9-Aug-90		On System Disk 5.0.3D17 Final CandidateThe first time, and only the first time during the time the driver isloaded into memory (until the app quits), a note alert is displayedbefore the either the page setup or print job dialog (whichever isselected the very first time by the user).A4 paper metrics size was wrong, causing wraparound graphics on righthand size.  Horizontal size was 132 16ths, changed to 136.D5		8-Aug-90Unable to fix clip/wraparound in some cases in AWGS/MSGS withMegafonts document.  This is a fundamental problem with apps notfollowing the model correctly.  All major word processing applicationsare not paginating based on the rPage/rPaper/iH/iVRes fields in theprint record; rather they paginate based on the printer type (iDev)and paper type fields, assuming that the output device will always be80x72 dpi, or an integer multiple thereof.  For the LaserWriter, whichisn't an even multiple of 80x72 dpi, the scaling is no problem, becausePostScript scales everything perfectly.  But for dumb printers whichhave a scaling model other than 80x72 dpi, the scaling must be donewith QuickDraw.  When we try this, we're asking QuickDraw to scaleeverything to 0.9375 of 1X/2X/4X.  The font manager gets it all wrong;many bad things happen: text overwriting, missing data, etc.  The realsolution is of applications to be written correctly.  In the mean time,I recommend we do NOT scale to 0.9375, and require that the useradjust his right margin manually in order to prevent clipping off theright side of the paper.  The other alternative is not to ship thedriver, but there won't be a fix forthcoming, not for 6.0, not ever.An alert dialog box comes up after "OK" hit on PrJobDialog if 300dpihas been selected on a machine with low memory.  The check is done withthe RealFreeMem call.  The dialog can appear after either the Job or theSetup dialogs.  Threshold set on RealFreeMem < 512K.D4		7-Aug-90Fixed blank line in between every DrawPicture rendering-page-imageband.  Was due to us assuming that we can do band-align-by-1 justbecause the HP can raster a single line at a time (not limited to atleast 16 or 24 like the IW or LQ).  However, QD patterns that alternatealso require alignment.  Therefore, the alignment factor has beenincreased set at 8 instead of 1.D3		6-Aug-90		Alpha candidate (with current feature set)Source code has been included in projector source control system so asto appear on system disk builds.  Added to build script and added toinstaller scripts.Most of the many different paper types have been removed.  The fourpaper types that will be supported are US Letter, US Legal, EuropeanA4 Letter, and #10 Envelope.The vertical condense dialog box popup text has been changed slightly.A hardcoded vertical line feed of 1/8" is now being performed tovertically center the printed page, since we don't support gap/no gap.There is a very serious problem where the printing model breaks downbecause 75 dpi is not an even number.  In our metrics model, we mustprovide the app with a value of 37.5 for iVRes.  Due to integercalculations, we are giving 37 for this value.  This causes verticalpage metrics to be off: in DrawPlus, the vertical margins count uptoo high, and it would be possible to go select VCondense and draw anobject which is flush to the bottom of the logical print area, and havean unwanted page pop up.  "Fixed" by rounding iVRes down all the time.This may be just a DrawPlus problem, and I have to see how the Laser-Writer driver deals with this issue.The imager is now aware of different paper types, including envelopes,by means of ImagerSetPaperType call.Fixed bug where we got an extra blank page in most cases.  Problemwas if the number of banding buffer passes in high level printloop isgreater than one, then we would get the extra page.  First, we weren'tinitializing the Gap bit in wDev anymore--fixed; second, we weren'tcalling ImagerSetLocInfo during the high level printloop's last-bandspecial-case set and during the restore ("lastbandheight")--fixed.Limited PrPixelMap call testing has been performed.  This driver willnot support printing a subset of the given pixelmap; but no applicationthat I know of does this.  The one app I know of that uses PrPixelMapis "Geometry".  (The PrPixelMap call is a way to cause printing otherthan the standard printing loop--almost no one uses it).Graytones in 320 mode have been improved by treating a 4-bit 320-pixelas two concatenated 640-pixel.  Pure-black and pure-white still workcorrectly, and for the values in between, an automatic dithering takesplace.  Result: arbitrary 320 graytones that look just as good as the640 graytones.Smart DrawPicture text clipping implemented.  Much less time spent in"Rendering page image"; 72% speed improvement on a typical page fullof text.D2		30-Jul-90		DevelopmentalThis driver will be an HP DeskJet PLUS driver.  At the present time,it seems impossible to communicate with Tabasco from a 'GS reliablythrough straightforward means.A competing driver seems to have come out from Bill Heineman.  Hisversion 0.8 appears to be very slow and does not seem to print 'GSfonts at 300 dpi (effective).  However, it *is* full-featured, andit is possible that a later version will print true 300 dpi effective.Trivial imager calls complete and imager interface fully defined.Imager pixel conversion/color pixel mapping method worked out,implemented, and tested.  Dithering for non-black/white colors willneed some improvement.Imager white-scanning and main converter loop implemented and tested.All imager calls fully operational.Imager compress-and-send routine implemented and tested.  The algorithmseems to work perfectly, yet throughput is somewhat disappointing.Code has been fully sanitized to be the HP DeskJet PLUS driver.Next perfomance task is smart high-level quickdraw DrawPicture textclipping.E1		14-Jul-90		ExperimentalNew-model printloop calls, which manage high-level interface thatthe application sees is working.  Verified operation with dummy imager.Everything related to old drivers except incorrect-dev-dialog code/datahas been removed.  Imager interface fully defined.E0		23-Jun-90		ExperimentalSee the file README for description.  This is an unauthorized skunk-works project at this time.Code converted over and much unnecessary stuff blindly removed.  Allcode needs to be gone over carefully in time.We need to: 1)establish 56K baud communication routines in thecommunication.aii source file and test; 2) theoretically define thestructure in the printloop.aii source file; 3) begin to write theimager.It has now been decided to write this, at least first, as an HPDeskJet driver.  Tabasco will only do 56K baud and it will be a whileuntil a 19.2K baud card is available for it.  Project seems to havesome semblance of blessing.  We will use the normal printer portdrivers, but network won't be supported.It is unclear whether it is really possible to talk to Tabasco;investigation will happen.  Project investigation now has backing.User interface is complete.